Hi Martin,

thank you, both for the Ack on the fan patch and for this.

On FSRM: on our GTX 560 Ti both 390.157 and 270.41.06 write the slowdown
factor to 0x020160 (0x020164 for hubk06) right before the 0x137100 mux
write and clear it right after. 390 also waits for the slowdown status
and then ~8 us on PTIMER before the mux write; 270.41.06 wraps only the
mux write itself. Without that bracket our GPC mux occasionally fails to
switch. The per-step map is docs/2026-10-25/core-reclock-map.md in the
repo.

The database: yes, very interested, thank you. Before you dig it out,
how would you like us to treat it? Our default would be to keep raw
traces and VBIOS images private and publish only what we derive from
them (register sequences, timings, per-board tables), with credit.

And since you noticed it in the other thread: yes, I work on this with
an AI assistant (Claude). It does much of the trace analysis and drafts
the texts; I run the experiments on my hardware and check what goes out.

I will ping you on #nouveau when I have a historical question.

Alex
